      "retrieval_hit_context_full": "Suddenly one of the covert ops groups shines a light on the group, demanding we tell them if we carry any meat with us.\nThe group has decided the best course of action is to take the Wolf to Stormspire Academy and see if someone can help cast Speak with Dead so they can learn more about the plans Wolf had.\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/Locations/stormspire_academy/\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/NPCs/wolf/\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/PCs/baergrom/\nWhen they enter the street outside they find it busy with activity.\nAfter Bonogo and Baergrom dump out hundreds of pounds of meat on the street the guards are quick to jump into action.\nAs the group continues on to the academy the tainted meat is burned up by one of the mages.\nThe group arrives at the Stormspire Academy and finds it bustling with activity.\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/Locations/stormspire_academy/\nThe group approaches the desk of a Half-Elf: Head Clerk Mossglade.\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/NPCs/mossglade/\nProfessor Cinderbranch is very interested in the events that led to Wolf's head ending up with the group.\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/NPCs/professor_cinderbranch/\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/NPCs/wolf/\nBefore departing with Professor Cinderbranch, Mossglade also tells the group about the \"study room\", a place the group can use to rest and recharge.\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/NPCs/professor_cinderbranch/\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/NPCs/mossglade/\nShe also tells the group that Torbin is in the infirmary under Professor Tealeaf's care.\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/NPCs/mossglade/\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/NPCs/torbin/\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/NPCs/professor_tealeaf/\nSo now the group must decide which to do first: visit the Necromancer to speak to Wolf, or head to the Infirmary to check on Torbin.\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/NPCs/necromancer/\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/NPCs/wolf/\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/NPCs/torbin/\nThe group decides to do both by splitting up.\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/PCs/baergrom/\nEphanna and Baergrom decide to go check on Torbin, while Karsemine, Bonogo, Stafl, and Caelynn meet with the Necromancer.\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/PCs/ephanna/\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/PCs/baergrom/\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/NPCs/torbin/\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/PCs/karsemine/\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/PCs/bonogo/\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/PCs/stafl/\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/PCs/caelynn/\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/NPCs/necromancer/\nWizards are busy making potions, crafting runes and working on wards.\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/NPCs/mossglade/\nWith a huff of impatience she asks how she can help.\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/NPCs/mossglade/\nBut as soon as they step outside the disheveled Council Chambers they are stopped by guards who were alerted to the Rune alarms.\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/Locations/council_chambers/\nLuckily Thalia is there to explain the situation and set the guard on alert for anyone with oily eyes.\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/NPCs/thalia/\nBonogo, not wanting to carry an entire body, removes the Wolf's head to take to the academy.\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/PCs/bonogo/\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/NPCs/wolf/",
      "lexical_hit_context_promoted": "Suddenly one of the covert ops groups shines a light on the group, demanding we tell them if we carry any meat with us.\nThe group has decided the best course of action is to take the Wolf to Stormspire Academy and see if someone can help cast Speak with Dead so they can learn more about the plans Wolf had.\nWhen they enter the street outside they find it busy with activity.\nAfter Bonogo and Baergrom dump out hundreds of pounds of meat on the street the guards are quick to jump into action.\nAs the group continues on to the academy the tainted meat is burned up by one of the mages.\nThe group arrives at the Stormspire Academy and finds it bustling with activity.\nThe group approaches the desk of a Half-Elf: Head Clerk Mossglade.\nProfessor Cinderbranch is very interested in the events that led to Wolf's head ending up with the group.",
