      "retrieval_hit_context_full": "Again the group decides it is best to split up and take care of two things at once.\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/PCs/baergrom/\nAfter Bonogo and Baergrom dump out hundreds of pounds of meat on the street the guards are quick to jump into action.\nProfessor Cinderbranch is very interested in the events that led to Wolf's head ending up with the group.\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/NPCs/professor_cinderbranch/\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/NPCs/wolf/\nBefore departing with Professor Cinderbranch, Mossglade also tells the group about the \"study room\", a place the group can use to rest and recharge.\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/NPCs/professor_cinderbranch/\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/NPCs/mossglade/\nThe group decides to do both by splitting up.\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/PCs/baergrom/\nThe rest of the group meet with the Necromancer.\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/NPCs/necromancer/\nWhen shown the head of Wolf they become very interested in helping.\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/NPCs/necromancer/\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/NPCs/wolf/\nWhile they get the ritual set up the group meets in the \"Study Room\" for a magical short rest.\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/PCs/caelynn/\nWhile taking this short rest Caelynn plays a wonderful song on her mother's pan flute.\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/PCs/caelynn/\nStafl and Bonogo will go meet the Necromancer for the ritual while Caelynn, Baergrom and Karsemine will hunt for the meat.\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/PCs/stafl/\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/PCs/bonogo/\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/NPCs/necromancer/\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/PCs/caelynn/\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/PCs/baergrom/\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/PCs/karsemine/\nWhen the group meets up again outside the room they discover that a piece of meat from Caelynn's bag escaped and is now on the loose in the Academy.\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/PCs/caelynn/\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/Locations/stormspire_academy/\nEphanna will stay with Torbin.\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/PCs/ephanna/\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/NPCs/torbin/\nStafl and Bonogo enter a basement morgue and find the head of Wolf in the center and the ritual about to begin.\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/PCs/stafl/\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/PCs/bonogo/\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/Locations/basement_morgue/\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/NPCs/wolf/\nAs with all Speak with Dead spells they are granted 5 questions.\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/PCs/stafl/\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/NPCs/necromancer/\nInstead of casting a spell they decide to perform a ritual.\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/NPCs/necromancer/\nEphanna and Baergrom discover that Tealeaf has been unable to help Torbin and has not been able to help work on potions.\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/PCs/ephanna/\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/PCs/baergrom/\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/NPCs/professor_tealeaf/\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/NPCs/torbin/\nThey decide to stay with Torbin while Tealeaf goes into the next room to work on potions.\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/PCs/ephanna/\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/PCs/baergrom/\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/NPCs/torbin/\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/NPCs/professor_tealeaf/\nSo now the group must decide which to do first: visit the Necromancer to speak to Wolf, or head to the Infirmary to check on Torbin.\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/NPCs/necromancer/\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/NPCs/wolf/\nLongmont Campaign/Campaign 1/NPCs/torbin/",
      "lexical_hit_context_promoted": "Again the group decides it is best to split up and take care of two things at once.\nAfter Bonogo and Baergrom dump out hundreds of pounds of meat on the street the guards are quick to jump into action.\nBefore departing with Professor Cinderbranch, Mossglade also tells the group about the \"study room\", a place the group can use to rest and recharge.\nThe rest of the group meet with the Necromancer.\nWhile they get the ritual set up the group meets in the \"Study Room\" for a magical short rest.\nWhile taking this short rest Caelynn plays a wonderful song on her mother's pan flute.\nWhen the group meets up again outside the room they discover that a piece of meat from Caelynn's bag escaped and is now on the loose in the Academy.\nProfessor Cinderbranch is very interested in the events that led to Wolf's head ending up with the group.",
